("What counts as a regular load?", "About half to two-thirds of the drum. Use one tab."),
("What counts as a large load?", "A full drum, bulky bedding or very dirty items. Use two tabs."),
("Do I need two tabs for a big load?", "Yes, two tabs for big or extra-dirty loads.†"),
("Can I use three tabs?", "We don't recommend it. Two is our max for a load. Overdosing can leave residue."),
("What happens if I use too much detergent?", "Extra detergent can leave residue and make fabrics feel stiff. Stick to the dosing guide."),
("What happens if I use too little?", "Clothes may come out less clean, especially very soiled ones. Bump up to the next dose."),
("What temperature should I wash with?", "Warm or cold, any normal cycle.† Follow your clothes' care labels."),
("Can I wash in hot water with Just 7?", "Yes, if your fabric allows it. Use hot for things like towels and bedding when the label says it's fine."),
("Does Just 7 dissolve in cold water?", "It's designed to break up in warm or cold water, with a light fizz to help.† For very cold washes, put the tab in first and don't overstuff. [Cold-water guide](/blogs/how-to/do-laundry-tabs-dissolve-in-cold-water/)."),
("Why didn't my tab dissolve?", "Usually an overstuffed drum, very cold water or a very short cycle. Put the tab in first, under the clothes, and leave room for them to move."),
("What if I find a bit of tab on my clothes?", "Rewash the item, or rinse it under warm water. Next time put the tab in first and load less."),
("Can I dissolve the tab in water first?", "Yes. For very cold or quick washes, let it fizz apart in a cup of warm water and pour it into the drum."),
("Does Just 7 work on a quick wash cycle?", "Yes for lightly soiled loads. For very short cycles, dissolve the tab in a cup of warm water first."),
("Can I use Just 7 on a delicate cycle?", "Yes. One tab, cold water, and follow care labels."),
("Can I use Just 7 on a heavy duty cycle?", "Yes. Use two tabs for big or very dirty loads."),
("Can I use Just 7 on a bulky or bedding cycle?", "Yes. Use one or two tabs depending on size and soil."),
("Can I use Just 7 with a steam cycle?", "Yes, if your washer's steam cycle adds detergent at the start. Follow your washer manual."),
("Can I use Just 7 with the sanitize cycle?", "Yes, if your fabrics can take it. Just 7 itself doesn't sanitize."),
("Can I use Just 7 on an eco or water-saving cycle?", "Yes. Leave room in the drum so clothes can move."),
("Can I use Just 7 with a prewash?", "Put the tab in the drum at the start. If you want detergent in both stages, dissolve a second tab in warm water for the prewash."),
("Do I need an extra rinse?", "Usually not. Add one for very heavy loads, sensitive skin or if you used two tabs. [Extra rinse explained](/blogs/home/do-you-need-an-extra-rinse-detergent-residue-explained/)."),
("Can I hand-wash with Just 7?", "Yes. Dissolve one tab in warm water in the sink first, then add clothes, soak, rinse and dry. [Hand-wash guide](/blogs/how-to/how-to-hand-wash-clothes-with-a-laundry-tab/)."),
("How do I hand-wash in a sink?", "Fill the sink with warm water, dissolve one tab, swish clothes, soak 15 to 30 minutes, then rinse until the water runs clear."),
